{"id": "EUVD-2026-80468", "enisaUuid": "fd0e6fa9-bc2f-3515-8feb-a2459f08d569", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmedia: chips-media: wave5: Add timeout while stop_streaming\n\nWhen stop_streaming is called, an infinite loop may occur in some cases.\nAdd a bounded poll of the queue status: loop until the queues drain,\nsleeping briefly between polls, and bail out once VPU_DEC_STOP_TIMEOUT\nelapses.", "datePublished": "2026-09-16T10:31:37", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:54:01", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/58e185e69a3dbe3494e54aad330f228f0b6645e1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c343348473e716882249bacf9297d6c363665fd9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c104f37b9f79d6c179c5f1a170d7f1da497ff527", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2ae7faed2e60d6d07d9efdd962d20dcb15330ced"], "aliases": ["GHSA-r4x2-4p88-7fm7", "CVE-2026-89868"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "099a2e8f-775a-3dab-8b83-7fc7a8f7f854", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "0ccd5015-2742-34af-9913-97c315edfb3e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.5"}, {"id": "0d1f018f-1cee-3591-a8f1-08b9ee9da11b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "516121ba-f9dd-3f6e-96ba-48b9de98af65", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9707a6254a8a6b978bde811a44fe07d86c229d1c <2ae7faed2e60d6d07d9efdd962d20dcb15330ced"}, {"id": "58b59bf7-e7b8-310b-9d71-b0ce1bb6e8c1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "604e010b-d21f-32f5-84b9-f1ddfc853ea7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9707a6254a8a6b978bde811a44fe07d86c229d1c <58e185e69a3dbe3494e54aad330f228f0b6645e1"}, {"id": "832b6c87-0098-38d9-8ae5